        "explanation": "<h3>Understanding Decimals</h3><p>A decimal is another way to write a fraction. It uses a <strong>decimal point</strong> to separate the whole number from the parts.</p><p>Example: <strong>3.75</strong></p><ul><li><strong>3</strong> is the whole number.</li><li><strong>.75</strong> is the decimal part.</li></ul><p><strong>Place Value:</strong></p><ul><li>First digit after dot: <strong>Tenths</strong> (1/10)</li><li>Second digit: <strong>Hundredths</strong> (1/100)</li></ul><div class='interactive-block'><h4>Try It!</h4><p>What is the place value of 5 in 0.5?</p><input type='text' class='form-control' placeholder='Type tenths or hundredths'><button class='btn btn-sm btn-primary try-it-btn' data-answer='tenths'>Check</button><div class='feedback'></div></div>",
